// Behavioral specification of a user-UUID value.
// Exists because an abstraction-owned method may only reference abstractions
// as influencing/influenced variables — never a concrete capsule.
// Protocol files carry abstractions only; the concrete UUID capsule belongs
// to the implementation layer, not here.
// Open: currently empty, so structural satisfaction is vacuous; decide whether
// it must require behavior (render/compare) before real implementers appear.
tp UserUUID ab

// Anything that can tell which user it belongs to.
tp Field_UserUUID ab

tp UserID mt (self Field_UserUUID) () (UserUUID)

// Register new user — TODO::: not yet designed; was a dangling comment in the Go source.
